title: 'Era points for blocks validators author on system chains'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-staking-async` gains `reward_system_chain_points`, a public function that credits
    points earned outside the relay chain to the active era. Accounts not exposed in the active
    era are dropped. Points from system chains and from the relay chain session report share one
    tally, so they also move the self-stake incentive share and count as activity for
    `chill_inactive`. The new `WeightInfo::reward_system_chain_points` must be added by external
    implementors of the trait.

    `pallet-validator-collators` counts the blocks each author produces as a
    `pallet_authorship::EventHandler`. Every `ReportPeriod` blocks it hands the counts of the
    authors in the stored validator set to the runtime's `BlockReporter`, in chunks of at most
    `MaxEntriesPerReport` entries, inside one storage layer. If the reporter rejects a chunk, every
    count is kept for the next report. Governance sets the period with `set_report_period`. New
    required config items: `BlockReporter`, `DefaultReportPeriod`, `MaxEntriesPerReport`. The
    runtime adds the pallet to the `EventHandler` of `pallet-authorship`.

    Adds `pallet-staking-async-system-chain-client`, which runs on Asset Hub only and receives
    the counts. Other chains call `report_authored_blocks` from `ReportOrigin`, which names the
    reporting chain, and the local chain credits its own counts through `credit_authored_blocks`.
    A count becomes `count × PointsPerBlock[source]` era points, handed to the runtime's
    `RewardPoints`. A source without points per block earns nothing. Governance sets the values
    with `set_points_per_block`, up to `MaxPointsPerBlock`. The client weighs a report by its
    number of entries, and each reporting chain bounds the size of what it sends.

    People Westend reports its counts to Asset Hub Westend over XCM. Asset Hub Westend adds
    `pallet-staking-async-system-chain-client` and credits its own counts locally.
    People sends at most `MaxEntriesPerReport` entries per report, and Asset Hub hands its own
    counts over in one chunk.
